    "https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/8382": {
      "title": "Office of Human Resources1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554",
      "description": "Fairmont State University Portal | Campus Police Officer Skip to Main Content Office of Human Resources 1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554 Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Police Officer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Working Title Campus Police Officer Type of Position Staff - Full Time Department Pooled Staff Position Appointment Length July - June (12 mo) Benefits Eligible? Yes Published Salary Requested Part-Time Staff Hours NA F.T.E. 1.00 Grant Funded Position? No If temporary (or grant funded) position, indicate ending date Description of Job Duties and Responsibilities Supports Fairmont State University by establishing and maintaining a safe atmosphere for the faculty, staff, students, and visitors by providing police and security services. Patrols campus in vehicle and on foot daily and during special events. Enforces all laws, regulations, and policies as needed. Works independently on a day-to-day basis under the supervision of a supervisor, but with the ability to deal with unusual situations as needed. General duties and responsibilities include but are not limited to: Serves as a preliminary and follow-up investigator; Patrols campus checking buildings and infrastructure for security issues and deficiencies which make the institution vulnerable to criminal acts; Patrols during special events, such as athletic events, concerts, etc. Directs traffic before, during and after the events; Provides crowd control which can include managing large numbers of people; Enforces all Federal, State, and Local laws, ordinances, and University regulations and policies; Enforces campus parking and traffic regulations; Makes arrests in accordance with departmental policies; Investigates traffic-related and general complaints; Testifies in court as needed; Watches for hazards and other dangerous or damaging situations; Administers first aid and provides or arranges necessary transportation; Provides police escorts as needed to protect property or people; Assists with the Fairmont State University Police Academy as needed; and Performs related duties as assigned or as directed. Minimum Required Education High School diploma or G.E.D. certificate Required Licenses and/or Certifications Valid WV Driver’s License Minimum Required Qualifications No experience or up to 6 months of experience; however, any equivalent combination of education and/or experience is acceptable which provides an applicant the listed knowledge, skills, and abilities and the capacity to perform the essential functions of the job. Preferred Qualifications West Virginia Law Enforcement Officer certification preferred, but not required Associate or Bachelor degree in Criminal Justice Enroll in a Police Academy program upon hiring Posting Detail Information Requisition Number 2026003SP Number of Vacancies Pooled Position Anticipated Hire Date Varies Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 06/19/2025 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Advertising Summary Quicklink for Posting https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/8381 Job Duties Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Certification/License Transcript #1 Transcript #2 Transcript #3 Contact Us For questions relating to Faculty/Staff positions, please e-mail the Human Resources Office at HR@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4111. For questions relating to Student Employment, please e-mail the Student Employment Office at studentjobs@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4836. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
