    "https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11810": {
      "title": "Purchasing Assistant",
      "description": "Fairmont State University Portal | Purchasing Assistant Skip to Main Content Office of Human Resources 1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554 Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Purchasing Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Working Title Purchasing Assistant Type of Position Staff - Full Time Department Procurement Appointment Length July - June (12 mo) Benefits Eligible? Yes Published Salary Requested Part-Time Staff Hours NA F.T.E. 1.00 Grant Funded Position? No If temporary (or grant funded) position, indicate ending date Description of Job Duties and Responsibilities The Purchasing Assistant supports the Director of Procurement and Assistant Director of Purchasing by coordinating essential purchasing, vendor management, and financial compliance activities. This role assists campus departments in navigating procurement processes and ensures adherence to federal, state, and institutional policies governing purchasing and vendor registration. Work is performed under the general direction of the Assistant Director of Purchasing and within established policies, procedures, and regulatory frameworks. This position requires independent judgment, strong analytical skills, and the ability to interpret and apply complex procurement laws, rules, and guidelines. The Purchasing Assistant interacts regularly with University faculty and staff at all levels, vendors, the West Virginia State Auditor’s Office, and the West Virginia Finance Division (wvOASIS). Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Provide guidance to campus departments on purchasing procedures, procurement methods, documentation requirements, and policy interpretation. Maintain tracking systems, logs, and records related to procurement workflows to ensure transparency, accuracy, and timely follow-up. Coordinate vendor onboarding activities, including collecting, reviewing, and processing required documentation; resolve discrepancies with vendors and state agencies. Provide administrative support to the Director and Assistant Director by compiling and maintaining contract-related documentation, monitoring key dates and deliverables, and assisting with the processing of renewals, amendments, and terminations. Maintain and update vendor records within University and State financial systems, ensuring accuracy and consistency. Process requisitions and issue routine purchase orders and service agreements; monitor status and communicate updates to departments. Serve as a primary point of contact for departmental inquiries regarding procurement processes, documentation requirements, and transaction status. Assist the Assistant Director in delivering training to campus departments on procurement policies, procedures, and best practices. Serve as a resource to faculty, staff, vendors, and external stakeholders regarding procurement policies and processes. Maintain and regularly update the Procurement webpage to ensure accuracy and relevance. Perform other procurement-related duties as assigned. Minimum Required Education Associate’s degree in business administration, accounting, finance, or a related field, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Required Licenses and/or Certifications N/A Minimum Required Qualifications Two to three years of progressively responsible experience in administrative, purchasing, financial, or compliance-related work. Strong communication, organizational, and customer service skills. Ability to interpret and apply institutional and state procurement policies and procedures. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications (Word, Excel, PowerPoint). Working knowledge of procurement principles, compliance standards, and documentation requirements. Strong organizational and time management skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines. Ability to communicate clearly and professionally with a wide range of stakeholders. High level of attention to detail and sound judgment when reviewing financial and contractual documents. Ability to analyze issues, identify discrepancies, and implement appropriate solutions. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in business administration, accounting, finance, or a related field. Experience with financial systems such as Banner and/or wvOASIS. Experience in purchasing, vendor management, contract administration, or PCard processes. Higher Education experience. Posting Detail Information Requisition Number 2027023SP Number of Vacancies 1 Anticipated Hire Date ASAP Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 08/27/2026 Job Close Date 09/10/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Advertising Summary Quicklink for Posting https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11808 Job Duties Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Certification/License Transcript #1 Transcript #2 Transcript #3 Contact Us For questions relating to Faculty/Staff positions, please e-mail the Human Resources Office at HR@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4111. For questions relating to Student Employment, please e-mail the Student Employment Office at studentjobs@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4836. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11828": {
      "title": "Office of Human Resources1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554",
      "description": "Fairmont State University Portal | Financial Reporting Manager Skip to Main Content Office of Human Resources 1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554 Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Financial Reporting Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Working Title Financial Reporting Manager Type of Position Staff - Full Time Department Accounting Appointment Length July - June (12 mo) Benefits Eligible? Yes Published Salary Requested Part-Time Staff Hours NA F.T.E. 1.00 Grant Funded Position? No If temporary (or grant funded) position, indicate ending date Description of Job Duties and Responsibilities The Financial Reporting Manager supports the financial operations of Fairmont State University by collecting, reviewing and analyzing financial data for external and internal financial reporting requirements. This role assists in producing timely, accurate and compliant financial reports while adhering to federal, state and institutional regulations and guidelines, maintains strong communication and relationships with the campus community and key financial stakeholders. Operational Duties: Internal Reporting – Assist with monthly, quarterly and year-end closing activities, including but not limited to preparing accrual entries, completing, reviewing and correcting journal entries, account reconciliations, and financial data to ensure the accuracy of financial information Collect interim financial data, identify significant variances, interpret data, and collaborate with the Finance team to compile monthly financial statements Create regular, recurring and ad hoc internal reports as needed to support university-wide decision-making Internal reporting includes but is not limited to financial statements, capital project budget reports, fixed asset reports and proformas External Reporting – Collaborate with Institutional Resources to complete all required and requested external reporting in compliance with state, federal and higher education reporting requirements for various third-party stakeholders External reporting includes but is not limited to Internal Revenue Service ( IRS ), National Collegiate Athletic Association ( NCAA ), Integrated Postsecondary Education Data System ( IPEDS ), Higher Education Policy Commission ( HEPC ) and the State of West Virginia. Audit Coordination – Assist Finance leaders with the preparation of the University’s annual audited consolidated financial statements, ensuring accuracy and compliance with policies, federal and state laws, Generally Accepted Accounting Principles ( GAAP ) and Governmental Accounting Standards Board ( GASB ) standards. Duties include but are not limited to developing workpapers, preparing schedules, creating and reviewing journal entries and collecting documentation. Audits include but are not limited to National Collegiate Athletic Association ( NCAA ), Research & Development (R&D) and Single Financial Audit ( SFA ) Process Improvement & Systems Optimization: Policy Development: Work with Finance team to evaluate, update, implement and document departmental and university-wide financial policies and procedures. Unit Collaboration: Collaboration includes but is not limited to, partnering with the Finance Team to ensure accurate and timely financial reporting and to ensure alignment between budget and actual reporting; and collaborating with departments across the university to promote clear understanding of financial data and processes Improvement: Drive continuous improvement by automating manual processes and enhancing ERP system functionality in conjunction with the State of WV’s ERP system Other: Participates in other projects and performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Required Education Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration or a related business field (or equivalent combination of education and experience). Required Licenses and/or Certifications N/A Minimum Required Qualifications 3-5 years prior experience with Finance, Accounting or Budgets, however, any equivalent combination of education and/or experience is acceptable which provides an applicant with the listed knowledge, skills, abilities and capability to perform the essential functions of the job High attention to detail and strong written and verbal communication skills Strong proficiency in Microsoft Excel (including formulas, data sorting, and pivot tables). Strict ethical standards for handling data confidentiality Preferred Qualifications Experience with higher education finances Experience with annual audit coordination Strong understanding of Generally Accepted Accounting Principles ( GAAP ) and Governmental Accounting Standard Board ( GASB ) Posting Detail Information Requisition Number 2027017SP Number of Vacancies 1 Anticipated Hire Date ASAP Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 08/20/2026 Job Close Date 09/10/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Advertising Summary Quicklink for Posting https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11768 Job Duties Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Certification/License Transcript #1 Transcript #2 Transcript #3 Contact Us For questions relating to Faculty/Staff positions, please e-mail the Human Resources Office at HR@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4111. For questions relating to Student Employment, please e-mail the Student Employment Office at studentjobs@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4836. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11842": {
      "title": "Assistant Vice President of Facilities",
      "description": "Fairmont State University Portal | Assistant Vice President of Facilities Skip to Main Content Office of Human Resources 1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554 Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Vice President of Facilities Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Working Title Assistant Vice President of Facilities Type of Position Staff - Full Time Department Facilities - Skilled Crafts Appointment Length July - June (12 mo) Benefits Eligible? Yes Published Salary Requested Part-Time Staff Hours NA F.T.E. 1.00 Grant Funded Position? No If temporary (or grant funded) position, indicate ending date Description of Job Duties and Responsibilities Job Description Summary: The Assistant Vice President for Facilities provides leadership and management oversight for all aspects of facilities, maintenance, grounds, custodial, construction, utilities, labor crews, and infrastructure. This includes the formulation of policy and standards, standards and procedures, safety practices, physical plant assessment, and occupational security standards. The AVP will foster a culture of process improvement and service orientation for the campus; evaluate and prioritize facility initiatives; and collaborate with stakeholders to further institutional strategic and operational goals to ensure the effective, efficient, and secure operation of all facilities. The AVP will be a creative and strategic leader, exhibit outstanding collaboration skills, and be an excellent communicator. The AVP reports to the Vice President of Finance & Administration and Chief Financial Officer. This position has been designated as essential. This means that when Fairmont State University is faced with an institutional emergency, employees in such positions may be required to remain at their work location or to report to work to protect, recover, and continue operations at Fairmont State University. Fairmont State University is an equal-opportunity employer and is committed to enhancing diversity among its faculty and staff. Duties and Responsibilities: The AVP has responsibility for all aspects of the institution’s physical plant, trades and services, custodial, grounds, occupational safety, construction, and deferred maintenance program as well as all related departmental budgets and staff. Specific oversight functions include but are not limited to the following: The AVP of Facilities will integrate into the Universities culture as a collaborative service provider and partner within all levels of the organization. Develop a service and student oriented mentality within the Facilities organization to support the strategic vision of the President and Board of Governors. Plans, sets priorities, identifies measurable outcomes, and oversees all major facilities functions and policies in alignment with the institution’s strategic initiatives. Drives a team environment within the Facilities Department, keeping customer service, student support, and accountability as primary directives. Establish and drive a maintenance and support culture to make all facilities and grounds a place of pride within the University community. Develop a robust preventive maintenance life cycle plan and recommend funding streams for the replacement of campus infrastructure. Facilitates professional training and development of employees; holds subordinates accountable for effectiveness, efficiency, and professional conduct; conducts effective searches by recruiting, hiring, training, evaluating, and motivating employees; participates in the administration of progressive discipline as needed; ensures good performance is rewarded; fosters an environment where all employees feel valued; promotes diversity, equity, and inclusion in all work units and decisions. Coach and ensure team development and training to ensure that best practices are implemented and support a culture of quality customer service. Oversees all capital construction and major deferred maintenance projects including development of RFPs, architectural design reviews, vendor management, quality assurance, system commissioning, invoice authorization, and warranty administration. Provides Directors, Team Leads, and other supervisors with expert technical support and guidance relative to various building systems and equipment; oversees the utilization of the computerized maintenance management system including monthly reporting. Recommends strategic and operational initiatives in support of the Strategic Vision which supports and advances the institution’s priorities. Authorize and oversee the deployment, monitoring, maintenance, development, and support of all facilities-based assets for institution-wide needs. Provide exceptional oversight with multiple vendors, including architects, engineers, and contractors, in coordination with all functional areas under the Facilities program. Supports and helps with the administering of vendor, consultant, and service contracts and ensures that Fairmont State University receives the full scope of service detailed in contracts. Prepare department annual budgets and administer funds according to budget approval. Explore, evaluate, and prioritize opportunities for automation, efficiency, cost reductions, and sustainability efforts. Collaborate with campus leadership in planning for disaster recovery and emergency responses. Maintains awareness of changing trends and regulations that may impact the institution and recommends or take appropriate corrective action as required. Other related duties as assigned. Minimum Required Education Bachelor’s degree in related field required Required Licenses and/or Certifications N/A Minimum Required Qualifications Seven years of senior leadership experience in facilities operations management with a demonstrated history of success in a maintenance organization, campus support, and capital improvement. Preferred candidates will have experience in higher education within the state of West Virginia. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Advanced knowledge and leadership abilities to move departments in the direction required to achieve the highest standards and support for the Fairmont State University’s faculty, students, and staff. Excellent communication and relationship management. Well-respected and trusted leader with integrity and transparency. Successful leadership experience in higher education. Demonstrated success in implementing and administering policies and processes in compliance with all regulatory requirements. Demonstrates effective budget, contract, and vendor negotiation and management. Demonstrated ability to lead and collaborate with diverse groups of people. Proven ability to work both independently and collaboratively, take initiative in the development and management of concurrent projects, and meet deadlines. Proven ability to maintain a broad organizational perspective and relationship with other departments to effectively carry out the internal and external relationships of the office. Dependability, flexibility, and willingness to oversee, direct, and respond to campus issues or outages during non-standard work schedules. Preferred Qualifications Professional Engineer or Certified Facilities Manager preferred. Posting Detail Information Requisition Number 2027026SP Number of Vacancies 1 Anticipated Hire Date ASAP Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 08/31/2026 Job Close Date 09/14/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Advertising Summary Quicklink for Posting https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11840 Job Duties Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Certification/License Transcript #1 Transcript #2 Transcript #3 Contact Us For questions relating to Faculty/Staff positions, please e-mail the Human Resources Office at HR@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4111. For questions relating to Student Employment, please e-mail the Student Employment Office at studentjobs@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4836. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11853": {
      "title": "Office of Human Resources1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554",
      "description": "Fairmont State University Portal | Admissions Counselor Skip to Main Content Office of Human Resources 1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554 Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Admissions Counselor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Working Title Admissions Counselor Type of Position Staff - Full Time Department Enrollment Management Appointment Length July - June (12 mo) Benefits Eligible? Yes Published Salary Requested Part-Time Staff Hours NA F.T.E. 1.00 Grant Funded Position? No If temporary (or grant funded) position, indicate ending date Description of Job Duties and Responsibilities Key Responsibilities: 1. Recruitment Strategy Development and Execution: o Develop and independently execute recruitment strategies for targeted student populations, including high school students, adult learners, and transfer students. o Plan and implement recruiting events such as college fairs, high school visits, and campus tours. These efforts will be guided by overarching enrollment goals and university priorities set by the Executive Director. o Evaluate the effectiveness of recruitment strategies within the assigned territory and make necessary adjustments based on data and feedback. 2. Student Engagement and Support: o Engage directly with prospective students and their families to provide guidance on the college application process, academic programs, and financial aid opportunities. o Provide one-on-one and group advising sessions for students, helping them navigate the admissions process, identify appropriate programs, and connect with necessary resources. o Serve as a trusted resource for students, offering ongoing support throughout the enrollment process to ensure they feel welcomed, informed, and prepared. 3. Admissions Operations and Event Coordination: o Working alongside the event coordinator-plan recruitment events within assigned territory, including campus visits, open houses, and information sessions. o Review and assess application materials for completeness, ensuring timely processing of student applications and corresponding communications. o Coordinate with academic departments and other campus offices to ensure that recruitment efforts align with institutional goals and meet student needs. 4. Strategic Reporting and Data Analysis: o Collect and analyze data related to admissions trends, student demographics, and recruitment outcomes to evaluate and adjust recruitment strategies within assigned territory. o Regularly report on progress toward recruitment goals, including analyzing application and yield rates, and presenting data to Admissions leadership for decision-making. 5. Professional Development: o Participate in professional development opportunities, including attendance at conferences and workshops, to stay current with trends in higher education, admissions practices, and student success strategies. Admissions Counselor Requirements: Experience in college admissions may be preferred. Familiarity with college and university programs, majors, admissions requirements and processes, and scholarship and financial aid resources. Excellent active listening, verbal and written communication, and interpersonal skills. Strong planning and people reading skills. Ability to multitask and stay organized. Willingness to guide prospective students and families and provide ongoing support as they make important decisions. Minimum Required Education Bachelor’s Degree required; Master’s degree preferred. Required Licenses and/or Certifications Valid Driver’s License with clean driving record. Minimum Required Qualifications Strong interpersonal, communication, and presentation skills. Proven ability to develop and execute strategic recruitment initiatives. Strong organizational and time management skills, with the ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously. Experience working with student populations, including non-traditional students and those from underrepresented backgrounds. Knowledge of current trends in higher education admissions and student engagement. Ability to work independently and take initiative in developing solutions to recruitment challenges Must be prepared to make frequent contact (inbound and outbound) via telephone, text message, e-mail, and other means with students and parents as well as internal and external audiences. Must pass background screening for access to and working within the education field. Must be willing to travel. Preferred Qualifications Goal and achievement oriented Able to multi-task, function well, and prioritize tasks in a fast-paced environment Able to create and maintain partnership with faculty, staff, and administration Exceedingly student service-driven Proficient in general computer tasks An advanced user of Microsoft Office and associated programs Able to carry and transport information materials (publications, marketing materials etc.) to various locations and events on and off campus. Excellent with public speaking and have refined presentation skills Able to coordinate multiple tasks and detailed events Able to communicate effectively with a wide range of audiences Excellent with organizational and planning skills Responsive to supervisor feedback and committed to continuous improvement Prepared for frequent overnight travel as required including evenings and weekend Able to rapidly acquire knowledge of admissions, curricula, and record policies & procedures. Willing to work independently as well as part of a team, and be accountable for deadlines and goals within an assigned territory or specific student population. Experienced and willing to work within a growth and change mindset A high achiever with excellent people skills Excel at initiating conversation with prospective students at college fairs and other events. Candidates with prior marketing, sales, or recruitment experience will receive priority consideration Key Competencies: • Strong leadership and team collaboration skills. • Ability to mentor and guide junior team members. • Excellent problem-solving and decision-making abilities. • Strong public speaking and presentation skills. • Proficiency in using admissions software and data management systems. Posting Detail Information Requisition Number 2027022SP Number of Vacancies 1 Anticipated Hire Date ASAP Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 08/27/2026 Job Close Date 09/18/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Advertising Summary Quicklink for Posting https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11800 Job Duties Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Certification/License Transcript #1 Transcript #2 Transcript #3 Contact Us For questions relating to Faculty/Staff positions, please e-mail the Human Resources Office at HR@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4111. For questions relating to Student Employment, please e-mail the Student Employment Office at studentjobs@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4836. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
