    "https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11792": {
      "title": "Presidential Events Office Assistant",
      "description": "Fairmont State University Portal | Presidential Events Office Assistant Skip to Main Content Office of Human Resources 1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554 Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Presidential Events Office Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Working Title Presidential Events Office Assistant Type of Position Staff - Part Time Department President's Office Appointment Length July - June (12 mo) Benefits Eligible? No Published Salary Requested Part-Time Staff Hours 1039 F.T.E. 0.49 Grant Funded Position? No If temporary (or grant funded) position, indicate ending date Description of Job Duties and Responsibilities The Part-Time Presidential Events & Strategic Initiatives Assistant provides administrative, logistical, and operational support to the Director of Presidential Events & Strategic Initiatives and the Office of the President. The position assists with presidential and university events, executive travel, purchasing, vendor coordination, communications, staff scheduling, mascot operations, and special projects. This position enables the Director to focus on executive-level event strategy, presidential priorities, strategic initiatives, and institutional relationships. Essential Responsibilities Administrative & Executive Support Maintain calendars, event files, contact lists, spreadsheets, schedules, and planning documents. Prepare agendas, invitations, itineraries, correspondence, meeting materials, and reports. Track deadlines and follow up with campus departments, vendors, and stakeholders. Organize electronic and physical records related to events, purchasing, contracts, and programs. Event & Program Support Assist with planning and execution of presidential receptions, ceremonies, meetings, community-facing events, and special programs. Coordinate RSVPs, guest lists, seating, catering, signage, supplies, event materials, and event-day logistics. Coordinate routine event details with campus departments and external vendors. Assist with setup and breakdown of events as needed. Purchasing & Vendor Support Assist with quotes, invoices, purchase orders, receipts, and expense tracking. Communicate with vendors regarding schedules, deliveries, event requirements, and logistics. Maintain vendor records and assist with tracking contracts and deadlines. Executive Travel & Special Projects Assist with hotel arrangements, transportation, itineraries, participant lists, meals, and materials for presidential and university travel programs. Support conferences, retreats, and multi-day programs involving university leadership and participants. Conduct research, gather information, prepare materials, and assist with special projects assigned by the Director of Presidential Events & Strategic Initiatives or the Office of the President within the scope of the position’s responsibilities. Communications & University Representation Assist with event invitations, promotional materials, social media, photography coordination, and event communications. Coordinate with Marketing and Communications to support university branding and messaging. Assist with scheduling and logistics for university mascot appearances and other university representation activities. Staff Support Assist with scheduling and coordinating student employees and part-time event staff. Communicate assignments, schedules, and event responsibilities. Assist with preparation and training of event staff. Minimum Required Education 4 year degree or equivalent encouraged Required Licenses and/or Certifications NA Minimum Required Qualifications Administrative, event planning, higher education, hospitality, communications, or related experience preferred. Strong organizational, communication, and time-management skills. Proficiency with Microsoft Office or comparable software. Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines. Professional demeanor and strong customer-service skills. Ability to maintain confidentiality and exercise discretion when working with presidential and university information. Ability to work occasional evenings and weekends for major events. Preferred Qualifications NA Posting Detail Information Requisition Number 2027021SP Number of Vacancies 1 Anticipated Hire Date ASAP Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 08/21/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Advertising Summary Quicklink for Posting https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11790 Job Duties Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Certification/License Transcript #1 Transcript #2 Transcript #3 Contact Us For questions relating to Faculty/Staff positions, please e-mail the Human Resources Office at HR@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4111. For questions relating to Student Employment, please e-mail the Student Employment Office at studentjobs@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4836. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11823": {
      "title": "Director of Global Education, Partnerships, and Immigration Services",
      "description": "Fairmont State University Portal | Director of Global Education, Partnerships, and Immigration Services Skip to Main Content Office of Human Resources 1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554 Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Director of Global Education, Partnerships, and Immigration Services Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Working Title Director of Global Education, Partnerships, and Immigration Services Type of Position Staff - Full Time Department Academic Affairs Appointment Length July - June (12 mo) Benefits Eligible? Yes Published Salary Requested Part-Time Staff Hours NA F.T.E. 1.00 Grant Funded Position? No If temporary (or grant funded) position, indicate ending date Description of Job Duties and Responsibilities The Director of Global Education, Partnerships, and Immigration Services provides leadership for the University’s internationalization efforts through the development and administration of international student services, study abroad programs, global partnerships, and immigration compliance. The Director serves as the university’s PDSO and primary institutional resource for international students and scholars, oversees compliance with federal immigration regulations, advances global engagement initiatives, and fosters an inclusive campus environment that supports international education. Reporting to the Dean of Honors and Global Education, the Director collaborates extensively with Academic Affairs, Student Affairs, Enrollment Management, Athletics, faculty, staff, and external partners to enhance international opportunities for students and strengthen the University’s global presence. Responsibilities: International Student Affairs Facilitates communication among international students, faculty, staff, deans, and administrators. Collaborates with Athletics to ensure strong support of international student athletes Coordinates international students’ start- and end-of-term airport transportation with Athletics, Student Affairs, Academic Affairs, Enrollment Management and other campus constituencies. Plans and conducts workshops on immigration-related topics for international students Collaborates with student clubs related to international education Inbound International Student Services Works with the Director of Orientation to develop and implement international student orientation programs. Provides pre-arrival information to international students Provides resources and advice to international students related to obtaining a driver’s license, state ID, bank accounts, etc. International Education (Study Abroad Programs and International Partnerships) Promotes strong partnerships with counterparts at universities, state (e.g., Global West Virginia), and national organizations (e.g., the Association of International Educators ( NAFSA ), Fulbright, National Student Exchange, the Institute of International Education ( IIE ), etc.). Develops and sustains robust relationships with international partner universities. Maintains accurate and up-to-date records of all international partnerships. Reviews and updates agreements regularly to reflect current terms and conditions. Coordinates dual-degree and articulation agreements and maintains established relationships with global partners. Facilitates enrollment in study abroad opportunities at Fairmont State for students at other West Virginia public institutions. Guide US students through the study abroad application process. Provides pre-departure orientation and re-entry support for study abroad students. Assists in health and safety protocols for study abroad participants. Provides emergency support and crisis management to students studying abroad. Conducts risk assessments for study abroad destinations. Facilitates faculty and student exchanges. Plans and conducts workshops on cross-cultural competence for US faculty, staff, and students. Acts as the primary liaison between the institution and international partners. Administrative Advises and assists international students regarding immigration matters, including, but not limited to: Maintaining visa status and compliance, Visa renewals and extensions, Changes in immigration policies and SEVIS alerts, Preparing and submitting required immigration documents, and Work authorization options ( OPT , CPT , etc.). Supports F-1 and J-1 Visa status students as well as F-2 and J-2 dependents by maintaining a working knowledge of SEVIS and immigration regulations. Oversees the generation, processing, and review of initial I-20s. Serves as Fairmont State University’s Primary Designated School Official ( PDSO ) with the Department of Homeland Security. Maintains Fairmont State University’s status as an SEVP -approved school and process I-17 for recertification. Serves an Alternate Responsible Officer ( ARO ) for the WVHEPC J-1 Exchange Visitor Program Consortium. Establishes institutional procedures to ensure institutional compliance with recordkeeping, retention and reporting requirements. Oversees office budgeting and accounting. Drafts and oversees processes related to global education. Supervise student worker(s) and/or graduate assistant(s). Engages in professional development to stay abreast of changes in the field. Develops assessment processes to align with university’s strategic goals for global education Prepares reports and updates for University leadership. Supports grant-funded international initiatives when applicable. Performs other related duties as necessary and as assigned. Minimum Required Education Master’s degree. Required Licenses and/or Certifications N/A Minimum Required Qualifications Working knowledge of education abroad programs, standards, requirements, and practices. Ability to work collaboratively across divisions to develop and sustain a strong university-wide ecosystem to support international students and global education. Strong multitasking, prioritization, and project management skills. A global outlook, cross-cultural competence, and intercultural communication skills. Ability to travel domestically and internationally. Excellent written and oral communication abilities. Enthusiasm and results-orientation Proven ability to lead and to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Commitment to customer service and student success. Proven ability to program development and management. Demonstrated proficiency in financial planning and budget management. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in a related field (e.g., Education, Higher Education, International Relations, World Languages, English as a Second Language, etc.). Previous experience as a PDSO or DSO Familiarity with federal immigration laws, regulations, and processes. Experience with the Department of Homeland Security’s Student and Exchange Visitor Information System ( SEVIS ). Understanding of National Collegiate Athletic Association rules and regulations that affect international student athletes. Proficiency in a world language. Experience studying abroad. Posting Detail Information Requisition Number 2027025SP Number of Vacancies 1 Anticipated Hire Date ASAP Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 08/27/2026 Job Close Date 09/27/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Advertising Summary Quicklink for Posting https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11821 Job Duties Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Certification/License Transcript #1 Transcript #2 Transcript #3 Contact Us For questions relating to Faculty/Staff positions, please e-mail the Human Resources Office at HR@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4111. For questions relating to Student Employment, please e-mail the Student Employment Office at studentjobs@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4836. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11829": {
      "title": "Office of Human Resources1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554",
      "description": "Fairmont State University Portal | Manager of Grant Financial Operations Skip to Main Content Office of Human Resources 1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554 Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Manager of Grant Financial Operations Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Working Title Manager of Grant Financial Operations Type of Position Staff - Full Time Department Accounting Appointment Length July - June (12 mo) Benefits Eligible? Yes Published Salary Requested Part-Time Staff Hours NA F.T.E. 1.00 Grant Funded Position? No If temporary (or grant funded) position, indicate ending date Description of Job Duties and Responsibilities The Manager of Grant Financial Operations supports the fiscal administration and financial compliance of Fairmont State University’s sponsored programs including federal, state and private grants, contracts and awards. This role provides grant financial data to key stakeholders including but not limited to leadership, the Office of Sponsored Programs, Principal Investigators and all granting agencies/partners as required or requested Operational Duties Manages the creation and closure of restricted funds within the University’s chart of accounts Maintains restricted funds by tracking expenses, allocating payroll, updating budgets, posting journal entries and performs budget-to-actual reconciliations for receipts and disbursements Prevents or corrects improper cost transfers and posting errors. Completes month-end processes for restricted funds and runs monthly financial reports and schedules Ensures a positive cash flow for restricted funds which includes but is not limited to timely invoices, completion of draw requests and required grant reporting Collaborates with Finance areas and Human Resources to create, calculate and balance grant funded positions Assists with the development of a streamlined cross-institutional billing workflow with Fairmont State Foundation Works directly with Fairmont State Foundation to invoice for reimbursements and reconcile grant funded requests Audit and Reporting Assists with year-end processes and audit functions for the annual financial audit, including but not limited to timing functions to prepare schedules, completing calculation and analysis, creating and posting accrual entries and providing support documentation as requested by the auditors for restricted funds Primary point of contact and coordinator for Research and Development audits Ensures compliance with all financial reporting obligations Assists with the completion of annual requirements for restricted funds including but not limited to Expenditure Schedule, Schedule of Expenditures of Federal Awards ( SEFA ) and Appropriation Requests for the State of West Virginia Process Improvement & Systems Optimization Policy Development: Work with Finance team to evaluate, update, implement and document departmental and university-wide financial policies and procedures. Unit Collaboration: Collaboration includes but is not limited to, partnering with the Finance Team to ensure accurate and timely financial reporting and to ensure alignment between budget and actual reporting; and collaborating with departments across the university to promote clear understanding of financial data and processes Improvement: Drive continuous improvement by automating manual processes and enhancing ERP system functionality in conjunction with the State of WV’s ERP system Other Participates in other projects and performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Required Education Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration or a related business field (or equivalent combination of education and experience). Required Licenses and/or Certifications N/A Minimum Required Qualifications 2-4 years prior experience with Finance, Accounting or Budgets, however, any equivalent combination of education and/or experience is acceptable which provides an applicant with the listed knowledge, skills, abilities and capability to perform the essential functions of the job High attention to detail and strong written and verbal communication skills Strong proficiency in Microsoft Excel (including formulas, data sorting, and pivot tables). Strict ethical standards for handling data confidentiality Preferred Qualifications Experience with federal, state, local, or private grant administration Strong understanding of Generally Accepted Accounting Principles ( GAAP ), Governmental Accounting Standard Board ( GASB ) and Uniform Guidance rules Posting Detail Information Requisition Number 2027013SP Number of Vacancies 1 Anticipated Hire Date ASAP Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 08/19/2026 Job Close Date 09/09/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Advertising Summary Quicklink for Posting https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11751 Job Duties Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Certification/License Transcript #1 Transcript #2 Transcript #3 Contact Us For questions relating to Faculty/Staff positions, please e-mail the Human Resources Office at HR@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4111. For questions relating to Student Employment, please e-mail the Student Employment Office at studentjobs@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4836. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11845": {
      "title": "Office of Human Resources1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554",
      "description": "Fairmont State University Portal | Accountant II Skip to Main Content Office of Human Resources 1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554 Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Accountant II Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Working Title Accountant II Type of Position Staff - Full Time Department Accounting Appointment Length July - June (12 mo) Benefits Eligible? Yes Published Salary Requested Part-Time Staff Hours NA F.T.E. 1.00 Grant Funded Position? No If temporary (or grant funded) position, indicate ending date Description of Job Duties and Responsibilities The Accountant II supports the financial operations of Fairmont State University by performing various accounting, budget or audit tasks related to capital projects and fixed assets Fixed Assets – Responsible for fixed asset process including but not limited to identifying, documenting, recording, reconciling, monitoring, and disposing of long-term physical assets, such as buildings, vehicles, equipment, and software Maintain the fixed assets subledger and complete postings related to gain or loss on disposal of fixed assets Collaborate with Finance areas to ensure timely and accurate reporting of fixed assets and ensure the fixed asset subledger reconciles with the general ledger Collaborate with the campus community to ensure all assets are physically tagged and any variances identified through the periodic asset tag inspections are identified and addressed Capital/Campus Projects – Responsible for capital/campus project process including but not limited to setup and closeout of project, documenting, recording, reconciling, and monitoring the financial performance of long-term projects like infrastructure, construction, and capital improvements including grant funded projects Maintain capital project funds and complete postings related to Construction in Process Collaborate with Finance area, project managers, facilities and operation teams to ensure timely and accurate reporting of capital/campus projects and ensure variances are identified and addressed Post and process journal entries and adjustments Assist with month-end and year-end closing processes, including gathering audit documentation and completing audit workpapers Maintain compliance with institutional policies, fund accounting guidelines, and standard regulatory frameworks. Post and process journal entries and adjustments Assist with month-end and year-end closing processes, including gathering audit documentation and completing audit workpapers Maintain compliance with institutional policies, fund accounting guidelines, and standard regulatory frameworks. Other duties and projects as assigned Minimum Required Education Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration or a related business field (or equivalent combination of education and experience). Required Licenses and/or Certifications NA Minimum Required Qualifications 1-3 years prior experience with Finance, Accounting or Budgets, however, any equivalent combination of education and/or experience is acceptable which provides an applicant with the listed knowledge, skills, abilities and capability to perform the essential functions of the job High attention to detail and strong written and verbal communication skills Strong proficiency in Microsoft Excel (including formulas, data sorting, and pivot tables) Strict ethical standards for handling data confidentiality Preferred Qualifications Experience with capital assets, projects or fund accounting Understanding of Generally Accepted Accounting Principles ( GAAP ) and Governmental Accounting Standard Board ( GASB ) Experience with capital assets, project and/or fund accounting Banner or wvOASIS experience Posting Detail Information Requisition Number 2027027SP Number of Vacancies 1 Anticipated Hire Date ASAP Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 08/31/2026 Job Close Date 09/14/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Advertising Summary Quicklink for Posting https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11843 Job Duties Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Certification/License Transcript #1 Transcript #2 Transcript #3 Contact Us For questions relating to Faculty/Staff positions, please e-mail the Human Resources Office at HR@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4111. For questions relating to Student Employment, please e-mail the Student Employment Office at studentjobs@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4836. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
